&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;I write about building AI agents and full-stack AI apps. Follow me for the next one, and tell me in the comments: Which planning pattern does your current agent use, and is it more complex than the task needs?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A CRM stores '10:30' beside a follow-up task. One representative reads it in Jaipur and another in London. Neither knows which timezone the value represents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Time data needs to describe either an instant or a local scheduling intention. Those are different requirements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Store instants unambiguously
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An enquiry acceptance time is an instant. Store it using a timezone-aware database type or an explicit UTC representation supported by your system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;JavaScript can serialize a valid Date as a UTC ISO string:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;acceptedAt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;timestamp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;acceptedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toISOString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This records the browser or server clock's value. For authoritative acceptance time, prefer the backend's timestamp and maintain its clock synchronization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do not infer an instant from an ambiguous string such as 06/07/2026 10:30.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Format for the reader
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Display an instant in an explicit timezone using a locale-aware formatter:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;display&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Intl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DateTimeFormat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;en-GB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;dateStyle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;medium&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;timeStyle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;short&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;timeZone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Asia/Kolkata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;acceptedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Choose the display timezone from a documented user or application setting. Label it where confusion is possible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Preserve scheduling intent
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;'Call tomorrow at 9 AM in the customer's timezone' contains more than an instant. Store the selected local date and time together with an IANA timezone identifier, then resolve it for execution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recurring local schedules need their timezone rules preserved. A fixed UTC offset does not represent future daylight-saving changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some local times occur twice when clocks move backward; others do not occur when clocks move forward. Ask for or document a resolution policy rather than silently choosing an arbitrary instant.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Keep audit fields separate
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Field&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Meaning&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Accepted at&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Backend accepted the enquiry&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Event occurred at&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Source reports when the event happened&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Received at&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Integration received the event&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Next attempt at&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Planned operational retry&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A delayed event's receipt time is not its occurrence time. Avoid overwriting one with another.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Test meaningful boundaries
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test different viewer timezones, month and year boundaries, daylight-saving transitions for relevant regions, invalid dates, and absent timezone settings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The conversion code above is illustrative and should be verified in your target runtime. Consistent timestamps make routing, follow-ups, and incident investigation easier because everyone can identify which moment a record describes.&lt;/p&gt;
